ermark-note"></p></div><div id="csm-uploaded-wrap" hidden><div class="csm-media-dates"><label for="csm-media-after">Uploaded from (UTC)<input type="date" id="csm-media-after"></label><label for="csm-media-before">Uploaded through (UTC)<input type="date" id="csm-media-before"></label></div><p id="csm-uploaded-note" class="csm-inline-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Choose a start date, an end date, or both. Includes originals and generated image sizes throughout the source library; both dates are inclusive.</p></div><div id="csm-media-browser" hidden><p class="csm-panel-intro">Click an attachment to toggle it. Shift-click to select a range. Space or Enter works with keyboard focus.</p><p id="csm-media-preview-note" class="csm-inline-status"></p><div class="csm-media-toolbar"><span id="csm-media-selected-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">0 attachments selected</span><div><button type="button" class="button" id="csm-media-select-visible">Select displayed</button><button type="button" class="button" id="csm-media-clear">Clear selection</button></div></div><div id="csm-media-list" class="csm-media-grid" role="group" aria-label="Source attachments"></div><div class="csm-media-toolbar"><span id="csm-media-page-status"></span><button type="button" class="button" id="csm-media-more" hidden>Load more attachments</button></div></div><p>Media files and attachment database records are separate. Include posts/postmeta when bringing over new attachments. The date-based option uses modification times; the comparison option uses cached checksums. Deleted files are not synchronized.</p></div></section>
        </div>
        <details class="csm-requirements"><summary>Connection requirements &amp; transfer limits</summary><p>Both sites need this plugin and 64-bit PHP 8.1+, cURL, writable private temporary storage, and writable selected destination files. Production connections require verified HTTPS. Endpoint: <code>?trickle=…</code>; requests use signed <code>X-CSM-*</code> headers.</p><p>This preview supports single sites and InnoDB tables without foreign keys. It transfers selected plugins, themes, tables and media, not WordPress core or wp-config.php. Destination URLs, Trickle credentials, and cron schedule are preserved. Plugin activation follows the source unless disabled. Database transfers can replace user accounts and other integration settings; keep destination login access and backups available.</p><p>Transfers use retained source streams and checksummed 512 KB network segments. Retry resumes at the destination checkpoint. Building the source stream and final staging can still hit hosting time limits; both sites need temporary disk space. Transfers stage privately and validate checksums before applying. The three most recent backups are kept on the destination. Rollback restores the earlier data and will overwrite changes made after applying.</p></details>
